---
// The privacy notice for vendors: wedding suppliers with a directory listing or
// a vendor portal account. It holds what the hosts' notice (`hosts.astro`) says
// about vendors, every part of that notice that applies to them as well, and
// what a vendor portal account holds, which the hosts' notice never covers.
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import PrivacyNav from '../../components/PrivacyNav.astro'
import { LEGAL_ENTITY, draftPending, isPlaceholder } from '@shared/legal'

// Highlight a detail only while THAT detail is still a placeholder. A page-wide
// flag would mark a filled field as pending the moment any other one wasn't.
const ph = (value: string) => (isPlaceholder(value) ? 'placeholder' : undefined)

// Name every field this page publishes that the shared identity check does
// not already cover. Leave one out and the banner can go while that field
// is still a token.
const draft = draftPending()
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy Notice for Vendors">
  {draft && (
    <div class="draft-banner">
      <strong>Draft</strong> — this notice is not final. Some details of the operator are
      still to be confirmed, and this banner disappears once they are.
    </div>
  )}

  <h1>Privacy Notice for Vendors</h1>
  <PrivacyNav current="vendors" />
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 2026-10-30</p>

  <p>
    This notice explains how <span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.name)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.name}</span>, trading as Cire
    (&ldquo;Cire&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;), handles
    personal information across the Cire service — this marketing site, the invitation site
    couples&rsquo; guests use, the organiser portal, and the vendor portal. Couples, co-hosts and
    organisers have their own notice, for <a href="/privacy/hosts">hosts</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vendor listings and enquiries</strong> — if you are a wedding
      supplier, the contact details on your directory listing (which for a sole trader
      identify a person), and the enquiry threads between you and a couple. An enquiry
      sends the couple&rsquo;s wedding name and message to the vendor they chose.</li>
    <li><strong>Site usage</strong> — the technical logs needed to keep the service secure. We run
      no third-party analytics or advertising trackers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="your-vendor-account">Your vendor account</h2>
  <p>
    You sign in to the vendor portal with your Musubi account, and manage your listing as a member
    of a Musubi organisation. Musubi describes your Musubi account in
    <a href="https://musubi.social/privacy">its own privacy notice</a>; this section covers what the
    vendor portal holds.
  </p>

  <h3>What it holds</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your sign-in</strong> — when you sign in, Musubi gives us two identifiers for your
      Musubi profile, and your handle, display name, picture and email address. We store them with
      a hashed copy of your session cookie.</li>
    <li><strong>Your organisations</strong> — when you use the portal, we ask Musubi which
      organisations you belong to, and your role in the one you are working in. We do not store
      either answer.</li>
    <li><strong>Your listing</strong> — the business name, description, service categories, email,
      phone number, website, Instagram, location and price guide, and the Musubi organisation it
      belongs to. A listing a couple created starts with the details they typed, until you change
      them.</li>
    <li><strong>Your claim</strong> — the email address each claim link was made for. While we check a
      claim, which organisation and Musubi profile made it, and when; once we confirm it, which
      Musubi profile claimed the listing.</li>
    <li><strong>Your replies</strong> — the messages and quotes you send a couple, with the Musubi
      profile that sent each one. The profile that claimed your listing is a member of each enquiry
      thread.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Why we keep it</h3>
  <p>
    To keep you signed in and show which account you are using, to show your listing to couples
    planning a wedding on Cire, to carry enquiries, replies and quotes between you and a couple, and
    to check that a claim on a listing comes from the business before we hand the listing over.
  </p>

  <h3>Who sees it</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Couples</strong> — once your listing is live, couples on Cire&rsquo;s Crimson plan,
      and the co-hosts who share their planning, can find it and see everything on it, your email
      and phone number included. When a couple adds your listing to their wedding or sends you an
      enquiry, we copy your business name, email and phone number into their own list of vendors;
      changing your listing later does not change their copy. The couple you reply to, and the
      co-hosts who share their planning, can read your replies and quotes. A quote is also saved in
      the couple&rsquo;s list of vendors, and they can add it to their budget.</li>
    <li><strong>Your organisation</strong> — every member of the Musubi organisation that owns your
      listing can see and change it, and read its enquiries and the replies in them.</li>
    <li><strong>Our staff</strong> — when you claim a listing a couple created, we check the claim
      before the listing becomes yours. To do that we look up your organisation&rsquo;s name and
      handle, your Musubi handle and your role in the organisation, and the email address on your
      Musubi account.</li>
    <li><strong>Our service providers</strong> — Cloudflare hosts the vendor portal and stores what
      it holds, and Resend delivers the emails we send about your listing, such as claim links and
      new enquiries.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Signing out deletes that device&rsquo;s sign-in record. In any case the session ends after
      seven days, and the record is deleted within a day of that.</li>
    <li>A claim link stops working seven days after it is made, and its record is deleted within a
      day of that.</li>
    <li>Your listing stays until it is removed. The portal cannot delete a listing: to have yours
      removed, contact us.</li>
    <li>What a couple keeps — their copy of your contact details, the enquiry, and any quote in
      their list of vendors or budget — stays with their wedding until they remove it or the wedding
      is permanently deleted.</li>
    <li>There is no set period for the messages in an enquiry thread: today they are not deleted,
      even when the couple&rsquo;s wedding is.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To provide the service — hosting invitations, collecting RSVPs, powering the planning tools.</li>
    <li>To send transactional email about your listing, such as claim links and new enquiries —
      never marketing without consent.</li>
    <li>To keep the service secure and improve it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information, and we do not use it for third-party advertising.</p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>We use a small set of service providers to run Cire:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, content delivery, databases, and infrastructure
      supporting security features such as rate limiting (global network).</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> — transactional email delivery, including vendor claim
      invitations.</li>
    <li><strong>Enquiries sent to you</strong> — an enquiry is sent to the supplier the couple
      chose, who then holds it under their own responsibility.</li>
    <li><strong>Grafana Cloud</strong> — service telemetry (metrics and traces; pseudonymised
      identifiers only, never guest content).</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — our pages currently load fonts from Google&rsquo;s CDN,
      which sees your IP address when they load. We plan to self-host these fonts.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We also disclose information where the law requires it. Our primary region is
    <strong>Oceania</strong>: our databases, which hold your sign-in sessions too, are hosted by
    Cloudflare in its Oceania region, and we operate from Australia. Cloudflare keeps read-only
    copies of those databases in other regions of its network, which it chooses and can change,
    and counts rate limits wherever in its network a request arrives. Some technical records
    &mdash; email delivery, service telemetry, payment processing &mdash; are handled by providers
    outside Oceania. If you are in the EEA or the UK, that means your information is transferred
    out of that area to Oceania and elsewhere; ask us and we will tell you what protections apply
    to that transfer.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    How long we keep your sign-in, your listing, your claims and your enquiries is set out under
    <a href="#your-vendor-account">Your vendor account</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Traffic is encrypted in transit, you sign in through Musubi, which uses passkeys rather than
    passwords, and session credentials are stored hashed. No system is perfectly secure, but we design for
    security first.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may have rights to access, correct, delete or port your information, and to object to
    certain uses — under the Australian Privacy Act, and for people in the EEA or UK, the GDPR and
    UK GDPR. To exercise them, contact us at
    <span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.contactEmail)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.contactEmail}</span>. You can also complain to a regulator —
    in Australia, the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC), or your local data
    protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use only the cookies the service needs to work (such as session cookies for signed-in
    organisers, vendors and guests). No advertising or cross-site tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.name)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.name}</span> (trading as Cire),
    <span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.postalAddress)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.postalAddress}</span> —
    <span class={ph(LEGAL_ENTITY.contactEmail)}>{LEGAL_ENTITY.contactEmail}</span>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
